WEBVTT

00:55.200 --> 01:02.770
"Time has passed since the end of the
great war between humans and monsters,

01:02.770 --> 01:06.810
and the people have sought prosperity

01:06.810 --> 01:10.180
by harnessing the primeval
power known as 'aer."'

01:16.690 --> 01:24.180
"Crystallized aer forms 'cores',
which serve to power 'blastia."'

01:35.600 --> 01:39.610
"Many different types of cores,
through the use of blastia,

01:39.610 --> 01:45.170
now provide us with all the
necessities for survival and prosperity."

01:46.650 --> 01:48.950
Magic and monsters...

01:48.950 --> 01:52.620
In this world ruled by powers
beyond human understanding,

01:52.620 --> 01:57.290
we are continuously faced
with decisions to make:

01:57.290 --> 02:03.890
What should we protect? What should
we give up? How should we live?

02:29.830 --> 02:31.660
Hold on! You're going too fast!

02:31.660 --> 02:33.930
Pick up the pace!

02:33.930 --> 02:35.920
Yuri! Over here!

02:40.770 --> 02:42.600
Okay! Next one!

02:44.610 --> 02:48.100
- How many do we have to set?!
- Our team's got three!

03:01.690 --> 03:03.180
Over here!

03:07.960 --> 03:10.300
- Let's go, Flynn!
- Right!

03:11.470 --> 03:12.830
Don't fall behind!

03:12.830 --> 03:15.000
Do you think the other teams will make it?

03:37.060 --> 03:41.660
Wait! We need to follow
the plan! Quit rushing ahead!

03:41.660 --> 03:44.100
We don't have time to wait around!

04:01.020 --> 04:02.620
They're catching up!

04:02.620 --> 04:04.480
- Go!
- They're all yours!

04:14.030 --> 04:17.990
No one said anything about these!

04:30.810 --> 04:33.680
Yuri! All done here!

04:49.100 --> 04:51.190
No way! How?!

04:54.540 --> 04:55.970
Has the operation failed?!

04:55.970 --> 04:58.630
No! Let's keep going!

05:18.560 --> 05:21.160
None of the other teams are even here yet!

05:21.160 --> 05:24.170
Shut up, will you?!
The plan's going just fine!

05:24.170 --> 05:26.660
What did you just say to me?!

05:36.340 --> 05:38.440
I'm a little scared now...

05:39.810 --> 05:41.980
Wow! There's a ton of 'em!

05:47.860 --> 05:49.150
Back this way!

05:55.200 --> 05:57.190
Took you long enough!

06:04.540 --> 06:06.170
Wh-What the?!

06:06.170 --> 06:08.340
What in the world?!

06:09.540 --> 06:12.180
Oh, man...

06:12.180 --> 06:14.150
Chastel! Everyone's here!

06:14.150 --> 06:15.680
Hisca!

06:15.680 --> 06:18.810
Yurgis! Get them back here!

06:22.060 --> 06:24.790
Yuri! Flynn! Come back!

06:30.300 --> 06:34.170
O brilliant light,
be as a wall to allay arms!

06:43.280 --> 06:45.140
Force Field!

07:28.460 --> 07:31.480
- Is it... over?
- Looks like it...

07:34.930 --> 07:36.620
Yuri!

07:38.600 --> 07:40.090
Flynn!

07:45.610 --> 07:49.600
Not too shabby for your first job!

09:57.440 --> 09:59.170
Yuri!

10:02.380 --> 10:04.180
What?

10:04.180 --> 10:06.810
Why didn't you follow the mission plan?!

10:06.810 --> 10:09.980
What's the big deal?
It all worked out in the end.

10:09.980 --> 10:13.820
We almost paid the price
for your selfishness!

10:13.820 --> 10:17.630
Get off my case!
You're too fussy about everything!

10:17.630 --> 10:20.460
You're too irresponsible, Yuri!

10:22.430 --> 10:26.100
Simmer down, you two!

10:26.100 --> 10:29.500
Now go take care of
the clean-up, on the double!

10:29.500 --> 10:30.710
Yes, Sir...

10:30.710 --> 10:34.710
- See?! He hit me, all 'cause of you!
- You're the one to blame!

10:34.710 --> 10:36.540
Shut up!

10:42.150 --> 10:43.950
Captain!

10:59.870 --> 11:01.800
Lambert...

11:06.370 --> 11:10.140
The red trees are rapidly
approaching the town...

11:17.820 --> 11:19.650
Aer...

11:48.150 --> 11:51.690
How long are you going
to stay dressed like that?!

11:51.690 --> 11:54.160
Just for a bit. No harm in that.

11:54.160 --> 11:57.160
Man, you're fussy... about everything.

11:57.160 --> 11:59.330
And look at this floor!

11:59.330 --> 12:02.130
Get off my case, will you?

12:02.130 --> 12:04.470
Talk about bad luck.

12:04.470 --> 12:07.800
Getting assigned to the same post...
and even the same room... as you...

12:07.800 --> 12:11.970
- Someone definitely has it out for me.
- That's my line!

12:11.970 --> 12:15.280
I still don't understand why
you would join the Knights!

12:15.280 --> 12:16.770
I'm coming in!

12:18.550 --> 12:21.150
What are you two doing?! It's time!

12:21.150 --> 12:22.380
I'm sorry.

12:22.380 --> 12:24.680
Hurry...

12:29.660 --> 12:33.430
This deserted in only a month...

12:33.430 --> 12:37.020
Business really dried up once
the monsters started appearing.

12:38.500 --> 12:41.100
You're late.

12:41.100 --> 12:43.440
I left Chris behind to wait
for you. Your shift's next.

12:43.440 --> 12:44.340
Yes, Sir.

12:44.340 --> 12:48.370
Yuri. Don't go tearing off
on your own like yesterday.

12:56.350 --> 12:58.050
Hey, you! Get back here!

12:58.050 --> 13:01.290
Seriously! Could you stop causing
trouble every chance you get?!

13:01.290 --> 13:03.320
Yuri can't help that he's so popular.

13:03.320 --> 13:06.360
Shut up! I'm sick of your snide remarks!

13:06.360 --> 13:08.260
Man, this thing's annoying.

13:08.260 --> 13:11.830
Don't be like that.
You're in charge of looking after Repede.

13:11.830 --> 13:14.170
Hey. Show me your magic artes.

13:14.170 --> 13:17.170
Huh? There's no need for that right now.

13:17.170 --> 13:20.310
I didn't see it yesterday.
I was face-down in the dirt.

13:20.310 --> 13:23.210
And they won't give us any,
since we're still rookies.

13:23.210 --> 13:25.650
I don't think they'll ever give you any.

13:25.650 --> 13:28.320
With your connections,
I bet you could get yours quick, Flynn.

13:28.320 --> 13:30.790
Your father was a Knight too, right?

13:30.790 --> 13:32.890
I'll obtain it through my own skill.

13:32.890 --> 13:35.190
Show me, for educational purposes!

13:35.190 --> 13:38.730
Only if you change your tone.

13:38.730 --> 13:41.660
Show... me... it... now... dammit!

13:41.660 --> 13:43.530
Are you trying to mock me?!

13:47.270 --> 13:50.340
Ugh, talk about lame!

13:50.340 --> 13:53.640
We specialize in healing and defense artes!

13:55.040 --> 13:56.940
Chastel!

14:00.650 --> 14:04.280
You can use blastia this way too!

14:10.860 --> 14:13.160
Oh!

14:14.800 --> 14:19.270
What are you doin'? That was dangerous...

14:19.270 --> 14:21.470
Captain!

14:21.470 --> 14:23.840
What are you doing here, Sir?

14:23.840 --> 14:26.340
I just checked out the forest.

14:26.340 --> 14:28.940
Now quit standing
around and go on patrol!

14:28.940 --> 14:30.380
Yes, Sir.

14:34.120 --> 14:38.190
Oh, Captain! Take this with you!

14:38.190 --> 14:42.020
It isn't much, though,
since we can't hunt in the forest.

14:42.020 --> 14:46.520
Sorry 'bout that. We'll have the forest
safe again as soon as possible.

14:47.630 --> 14:51.030
I'm going to see Garista.
I leave the rest to you.

14:51.030 --> 14:53.030
- Yes, Sir.
- O-Oh, Captain!

14:53.030 --> 14:55.140
Take Repede with you.

14:55.140 --> 14:57.430
He's a real nuisance.

14:58.610 --> 15:00.160
Lambert.

15:01.310 --> 15:03.540
- See you later.
- Yeah.

15:07.380 --> 15:10.520
Captain! I finished what you asked for!

15:10.520 --> 15:12.950
Oh! Toss it down!

15:14.020 --> 15:15.960
Thanks a bunch!

15:15.960 --> 15:17.890
He's sure buddy-buddy with everyone...

15:17.890 --> 15:21.000
This would never happen
with Knights in the capital...

15:21.000 --> 15:25.470
Well, it is a small town.
We all gotta work together.

15:25.470 --> 15:30.710
But it's also true that he isn't
a typical Knight captain.

15:30.710 --> 15:35.340
Making the forest safe soon...
He promises too much!

15:57.000 --> 15:58.970
Garista!

16:04.770 --> 16:06.940
Captain Fedrok.

16:06.940 --> 16:08.700
Hey there, Garista!

16:10.040 --> 16:12.980
Please keep your voice down in the library.

16:12.980 --> 16:15.810
I want your opinion on somethin'!

16:17.390 --> 16:21.690
It appears you've subdued
most of the monsters in the forest.

16:21.690 --> 16:24.160
All thanks to your strategy.

16:24.990 --> 16:29.860
We noticed an unusual
amount of aer there, though.

16:29.860 --> 16:33.030
It has the plants and animals going crazy.

16:33.030 --> 16:37.100
You believe aer is behind
the sudden surge in monsters?

16:37.100 --> 16:39.670
And the unseasonal red foliage?

16:39.670 --> 16:44.480
Our blastia acted up
during the mission, too.

16:44.480 --> 16:49.980
You're saying there's so much aer
spewing out that it affects blastia?

16:49.980 --> 16:54.860
There's no point in subduing these
monsters until we stop it first.

16:54.860 --> 16:57.360
Where could it be coming from?

16:57.360 --> 17:01.100
You know those ruins in the lake upriver?

17:01.100 --> 17:03.600
Seeing as the red trees
are following the river,

17:03.600 --> 17:05.600
I wonder if there's something there...

17:05.600 --> 17:10.260
Something that's releasing aer, you mean?

17:11.510 --> 17:15.440
Some sort of blastia, perhaps?

17:17.310 --> 17:22.550
The place was abandoned,
though. It should be empty.

17:22.550 --> 17:25.140
We'll need to investigate quickly.

17:25.950 --> 17:28.060
A mandate has arrived
from the imperial capital.

17:28.060 --> 17:30.160
You're to attend the
ceremony three days from now

17:30.160 --> 17:33.350
celebrating the tenth anniversary
of the end of the Great War.

17:36.530 --> 17:41.330
Our job ain't to stand
in lines all formal-like.

17:43.800 --> 17:47.270
If only it were that easy
to tell that to Headquarters.

17:47.270 --> 17:50.850
If you're going to attend,
you'll need to leave soon.

17:50.850 --> 17:56.680
Say, do you know any
aer or blastia experts?

17:56.680 --> 17:59.890
I believe there's a laboratory nearby

17:59.890 --> 18:03.620
belonging to a blastia
researcher named Rita Mordio.

18:03.620 --> 18:05.360
Tell me where it is.

18:05.360 --> 18:08.160
You plan to go there?
What about the ceremony?

18:08.160 --> 18:10.100
I'll send someone else.

18:12.100 --> 18:15.100
But what about His Excellency
Commandant Alexei?!

18:15.100 --> 18:18.770
I deem this far more urgent.

18:21.380 --> 18:26.150
Very well. But there is one issue...

18:26.150 --> 18:29.950
Mordio tends to be a bit... difficult.

18:29.950 --> 18:33.510
You might want to take
a present with you...

18:52.540 --> 18:54.210
Our shift's finally over...

18:54.210 --> 18:57.340
It's exhausting, being so on-edge lately.

18:57.340 --> 18:59.540
All right. In that case...

19:00.880 --> 19:03.620
What are you doing?

19:03.620 --> 19:05.350
Let's stop by later!

19:07.720 --> 19:10.830
I'll pass.

19:10.830 --> 19:12.990
Too good to hang out with us?!

19:12.990 --> 19:15.330
He's never going to make it big.

19:20.530 --> 19:22.800
Oh, no. The guild's here...

19:22.800 --> 19:24.710
Talk about bad timing...

19:24.710 --> 19:26.340
What's a guild?

19:26.340 --> 19:29.110
I'm sure you had them in the lower
quarter of the capital, too.

19:29.110 --> 19:32.510
They act like vigilantes and
only care about making money.

19:32.510 --> 19:34.880
They're part of a bigger
group called the Union,

19:34.880 --> 19:37.850
led by Don Whitehorse.

19:37.850 --> 19:40.550
They're a nasty bunch, basically.

19:45.530 --> 19:47.460
Hold on, Yuri!

19:48.630 --> 19:52.830
The guy wanted to get to the town
on the other side of the forest,

19:52.830 --> 19:56.500
so I told 'im to give me
all his money up front!

19:57.510 --> 19:59.370
Don't do it, Yuri.

20:00.670 --> 20:02.200
Welcome!

20:03.110 --> 20:07.600
Two Mabo Curries. Oh, and some milk.

20:09.950 --> 20:12.210
Oh, how cute!

20:13.790 --> 20:15.690
Is this little one a member too?

20:15.690 --> 20:17.690
Officially, not yet.

20:17.690 --> 20:20.290
Just a minute, okay?

20:20.290 --> 20:22.430
It was a pain in the ass, though,

20:22.430 --> 20:25.470
so I ditched the geezer the
minute we got outta the forest!

20:25.470 --> 20:30.170
That wasn't nice. You were supposed
to guard him all the way to town.

20:32.370 --> 20:35.710
Scamming people by doing a crappy
job and then boozing it up...

20:35.710 --> 20:37.800
You're one upstanding guy, all right.

20:46.490 --> 20:50.460
Yo. You got some real spunk, Mr. Knight.

20:50.460 --> 20:53.460
Let's see you say that
to my face this time!

20:53.460 --> 20:56.300
You two-bit thugs are all alike.

20:56.300 --> 20:57.460
Eh?!

20:57.460 --> 21:00.470
Not so close.
I'm not looking for a boyfriend.

21:00.470 --> 21:02.530
Why, you little!

21:28.200 --> 21:30.930
Go stop them, Flynn...

21:30.930 --> 21:33.600
Yuri started it.

21:33.600 --> 21:36.000
It has nothing to do with...

21:36.000 --> 21:38.170
Don't act all big!

21:38.170 --> 21:41.270
I just said this has
nothing to do with me!

21:49.180 --> 21:51.810
- Whoa!
- Here we go!

21:59.190 --> 22:01.460
Who the hell are you?!

22:03.700 --> 22:05.160
Hey!

22:26.150 --> 22:27.220
Bastard!

22:27.220 --> 22:28.880
Enough!

22:39.000 --> 22:42.440
You would dare draw a blade in here?!

22:44.440 --> 22:46.800
B-But, Sir...

22:48.210 --> 22:50.110
Sorry!

22:58.990 --> 23:04.320
You've got balls. It's too bad
you're one of the Empire's dogs.

23:06.190 --> 23:11.500
I'm Merzhom Keida.
I run the guild in this town.

23:11.500 --> 23:15.440
Yuri. Yuri Lowell.

23:15.440 --> 23:21.540
Work's all but dried up lately.
Has everyone high-strung.

23:21.540 --> 23:25.210
I'll make sure they see
their jobs all the way through,

23:25.210 --> 23:30.550
so I personally ask that
you excuse their behavior.

23:30.550 --> 23:33.210
Sure thing, Pops!

23:36.860 --> 23:40.990
These monsters lately
definitely ain't normal.

23:40.990 --> 23:42.600
Nope.

23:42.600 --> 23:47.030
They never used to go
near towns with barriers.

23:47.030 --> 23:49.270
What is that bum Niren doing?

23:49.270 --> 23:51.370
Niren?

23:51.370 --> 23:53.510
Oh, you mean the captain?

23:53.510 --> 23:55.610
Sounds like you're on pretty close terms.

23:55.610 --> 23:58.450
It's a boring ol' story.

23:58.450 --> 24:01.220
I hear you conducted
a large-scale monster extermination

24:01.220 --> 24:02.880
in the forest yesterday.

24:02.880 --> 24:04.020
Yeah.

24:04.020 --> 24:07.650
There are unseasonal
red trees in the forest, too.

24:07.650 --> 24:10.560
Seems likely there's
some sorta connection, huh?

24:10.560 --> 24:14.360
Dunno. But the captain seems to think so.

24:14.360 --> 24:16.630
He's consulting with our strategist.

24:18.330 --> 24:21.370
- Keep your big mouth shut!
- You idiot!

24:21.370 --> 24:24.100
- Let's go!
- Oww!

24:24.100 --> 24:27.310
I'm not done eating! Hey!

24:27.310 --> 24:30.280
Let go! That hurts!

24:31.880 --> 24:34.280
Okay! Okay!

24:38.290 --> 24:40.150
Raven!

24:45.190 --> 24:48.130
New job for you.

24:51.330 --> 24:56.170
What?! Why does he get
healing artes?! This is discrimination!

24:56.170 --> 24:57.470
Shut up!

24:58.810 --> 25:01.440
Let that be a lesson to you!

25:01.440 --> 25:03.980
- I feel sorry for you, Flynn.
- You're so cold-hearted with me!

25:03.980 --> 25:06.210
- But only a little bit.
- Show some respect! I'm older than you!

25:06.210 --> 25:11.690
Oh, your head is hurt too. Let me see.

25:11.690 --> 25:13.990
Stay still!

25:13.990 --> 25:17.690
Why would someone like you
join the Knights anyway?!

25:17.690 --> 25:22.100
No real reason. Nothing else
to do, and the pay is decent.

25:22.100 --> 25:24.660
Plus, I'm tough.

25:26.370 --> 25:31.670
In other words, he was wandering around
aimlessly, just itching for action.

25:31.670 --> 25:32.770
Shut up!

25:32.770 --> 25:35.640
He's the same as always!
He hasn't matured one bit!

25:35.640 --> 25:40.610
Same for you! Your nasty
personality hasn't changed at all!

25:40.610 --> 25:42.150
Childhood friends?

25:42.150 --> 25:46.290
We grew up together in the lower
quarter of the capital, that's all!

25:46.290 --> 25:49.690
It was like a dream come true
when you finally moved away.

25:49.690 --> 25:53.290
And I doubted my eyes when
I saw you at the recruitment exam!

25:53.290 --> 25:54.660
Why did you join?!

25:54.660 --> 25:58.130
Dunno, maybe your old
man rubbed off on me.

25:58.130 --> 26:00.100
He was one great guy.

26:00.100 --> 26:05.340
I was a little jealous,
not having parents of my own...

26:05.340 --> 26:07.600
Don't talk about him.

26:11.610 --> 26:16.380
You four. Go see the
captain when you're done.

26:16.380 --> 26:18.680
He's fuming!

26:19.950 --> 26:24.060
What for?!
We didn't do anything wrong!

26:24.060 --> 26:26.560
We're members of the Knights,
if you haven't forgotten!

26:26.560 --> 26:28.630
There's a little thing called "discipline"!

26:28.630 --> 26:34.590
Oh, man! My ability to supervise you
is gonna be called into question!

26:38.340 --> 26:42.640
Brawling in a pub...
Now that's some mundane stupidity...

26:43.610 --> 26:45.270
I'm sorry, Sir.

26:46.310 --> 26:49.480
It's crazy enough as it is outside the town.

26:49.480 --> 26:52.390
Don't make things any worse on the inside.

26:52.390 --> 26:55.520
But they were way out of line!

26:55.520 --> 27:00.060
They took an old man's money
and then just ditched him!

27:00.060 --> 27:02.360
I had to teach 'em a lesson!

27:02.360 --> 27:04.460
I see.

27:04.460 --> 27:08.830
Yeah, I probably would've beat 'em up too.

27:10.140 --> 27:14.840
But the guilds are autonomous
groups, free from imperial influence.

27:14.840 --> 27:17.210
They have their good aspects, too.

27:17.210 --> 27:20.480
I find that difficult to believe...

27:20.480 --> 27:26.150
I'm sure you realize by now that
they're handling things that we can't.

27:26.150 --> 27:28.990
For a price, though, of course.

27:28.990 --> 27:32.160
Some guy called Merzhom
seemed to know you.

27:32.160 --> 27:36.530
Hmm? Oh, yes. It's a boring ol' story.

27:38.670 --> 27:40.030
What?!

27:40.030 --> 27:43.870
We're not doing business under
the table, if that's what you're thinking!

27:43.870 --> 27:46.540
- Are your injuries all better?
- Yes, Sir...

27:46.540 --> 27:49.280
Then go back to your quarters.

27:49.280 --> 27:50.470
Huh?

27:52.010 --> 27:55.620
You're not gonna toss us in the stockade?

27:55.620 --> 27:59.280
What good would that do now?

28:01.520 --> 28:04.520
That said, I suppose
letting you off the hook

28:04.520 --> 28:08.630
would serve as a bad
example for the others...

28:08.630 --> 28:12.690
I'll dock the pub's repair
costs from your pay.

28:13.970 --> 28:17.940
Oh, and Flynn. I'm sending
you to the imperial capital.

28:17.940 --> 28:19.040
Sir?

28:19.040 --> 28:22.110
- You'll be filling in for me.
- I will?!

28:22.110 --> 28:24.950
I have somewhere else to be.

28:24.950 --> 28:27.950
In the meantime, Yurgis is in charge here.

28:27.950 --> 28:35.160
You're to attend the ceremony and
deliver this request for reinforcements.

28:35.160 --> 28:38.730
I think something's going
on in those lake ruins.

28:38.730 --> 28:43.300
But we lack the manpower
to handle it on our own.

28:43.300 --> 28:46.600
Oh, and the "bigger"
girl will accompany me.

28:46.600 --> 28:49.760
- That's sexual harassment, isn't it?
- It is.

28:51.870 --> 28:55.670
Bigger? But they're both
the same height. Right?

28:57.980 --> 29:02.850
- You're to look after Lambert, Yuri.
- Again with the dogs?!

29:12.560 --> 29:14.290
Yuri.

29:14.290 --> 29:15.760
What?

29:15.760 --> 29:19.530
Don't cause any more trouble.
I'm tired of getting dragged into it.

29:19.530 --> 29:21.170
Yeah, yeah...

29:21.170 --> 29:23.640
You're a member of the Knights.

29:23.640 --> 29:26.610
You need to obey the
rules and regulations.

29:26.610 --> 29:30.010
If you can't do that,
then you don't belong here.

29:30.010 --> 29:33.210
I don't feel I've done anything wrong!

29:33.210 --> 29:38.520
Just leave, if you're going to put your
own ideas before all else like that!

29:39.850 --> 29:41.840
Get off my case.

30:54.190 --> 30:58.530
- I take it we're lost?
- We're lost.

30:59.630 --> 31:01.860
Can't make heads or tails of it...

31:02.770 --> 31:06.210
He calls these scribbles a map?

31:06.210 --> 31:10.010
Sir Garista's so cool, too. This is a shock...

31:11.110 --> 31:14.340
Chastel! In the grass!

31:18.220 --> 31:20.820
Looks like an alarm. Check it out!

31:20.820 --> 31:21.810
Yes, Sir!

31:36.340 --> 31:38.000
Thataway!

31:43.840 --> 31:45.610
The imperial capital...

32:30.620 --> 32:32.890
This is a lab?

32:32.890 --> 32:35.160
Apparently so...

32:40.870 --> 32:44.430
Hey! Anyone here?

33:01.720 --> 33:04.190
Get lost...

33:06.630 --> 33:07.730
Wait!

33:07.730 --> 33:09.790
...you thieves!

33:25.880 --> 33:28.370
What, is she half-asleep or something?

33:42.600 --> 33:45.030
A-A child?!

33:56.980 --> 33:58.950
Not so fast.

33:58.950 --> 34:00.710
Rita Mordio, yes?

34:00.710 --> 34:05.690
We're Niren Fedrok and
Chastel Aiheap of the Imperial Knights.

34:05.690 --> 34:08.210
This is our bargaining chip.

34:09.290 --> 34:11.790
What do you want to know?

34:11.790 --> 34:14.330
We've detected a large amount
of aer being produced

34:14.330 --> 34:16.660
in the forest near Ceazontania.

34:16.660 --> 34:22.100
So much, in fact, that it's affecting plants
and gentle creatures in the area.

34:22.100 --> 34:27.270
It seems kinda strange for aer to
produce such effects all by itself...

34:27.270 --> 34:28.540
Meaning?

34:28.540 --> 34:30.780
Just a sec...

34:30.780 --> 34:32.850
Ceazontania...

34:32.850 --> 34:35.780
There are some ruins
on the lake upstream...

34:35.780 --> 34:39.850
Oh, I've scoped that place out before.

34:39.850 --> 34:43.890
But the barrier blastia
there was missing its core.

34:43.890 --> 34:47.460
The blastia isn't active, then?

34:47.460 --> 34:53.700
Nope! And I'm pretty sure there
wasn't an aer krene there, either...

34:53.700 --> 34:56.000
Aer krene?

34:56.000 --> 34:59.540
Kinda like a spring,
but with aer instead of water.

34:59.540 --> 35:03.780
Aer flows through the land so
you can find it pretty much anywhere,

35:03.780 --> 35:06.450
but there are some places
where it really gushes out of.

35:06.450 --> 35:10.380
But if it's suddenly producing
large amounts of aer now,

35:10.380 --> 35:14.950
then it's possible someone inserted
a core into the blastia to activate it...

35:14.950 --> 35:21.030
And maybe it's out of control
and spewing out the aer...

35:21.030 --> 35:25.000
Blastia are useful for
generating all kinds of power,

35:25.000 --> 35:29.470
but they become dangerous
when used improperly.

35:29.470 --> 35:34.840
Assuming this blastia is active,
would it be possible to destroy it?

35:34.840 --> 35:38.650
Can't really say without knowing
what kind of core it has...

35:38.650 --> 35:41.480
Isn't there anything we can do?

35:41.480 --> 35:45.520
- I take it this aer is red?
- Yeah.

35:45.520 --> 35:47.320
It's too concentrated.

35:47.320 --> 35:50.290
If oversaturation is
affecting the surroundings,

35:50.290 --> 35:54.560
then you'll first need
to stop it at its source...

35:54.560 --> 35:56.690
Just a minute!

36:00.130 --> 36:01.630
Here.

36:01.630 --> 36:07.000
I built this little one to collect aer.
She might be able to clear it up.

36:07.770 --> 36:09.010
How does it work?

36:09.010 --> 36:12.550
Set her down and activate
her near the source of the aer.

36:12.550 --> 36:15.720
She'll do the rest on her own.

36:15.720 --> 36:17.950
I can't guarantee she'll prove useful.

36:17.950 --> 36:21.990
She's a blastia, so she
might be affected too.

36:21.990 --> 36:24.690
Plus, this is all just a theory.

36:24.690 --> 36:26.890
Exactly.

36:30.460 --> 36:32.160
Thanks.

36:36.170 --> 36:40.970
I've been looking everywhere for this core!

36:40.970 --> 36:44.140
Wait, how'd you find me, anyway?

36:44.140 --> 36:46.450
One of my men, Garista, told me.

36:46.450 --> 36:48.620
Ah.

36:48.620 --> 36:51.220
Yeah, I hate him.

36:51.220 --> 36:52.690
You're on close terms?

36:52.690 --> 36:56.060
Heck, no! I only met
him before in the capital!

36:56.060 --> 36:57.660
He's a real jerk!

36:57.660 --> 36:59.690
Huh? Are you sure?

36:59.690 --> 37:04.860
He took the cores I found
and turned them into weapons!

37:06.000 --> 37:11.640
The stupid Empire only
sees blastia as tools for war!

37:11.640 --> 37:13.470
Just a minute.

37:25.720 --> 37:30.360
Here. This formula will make your
blastia immune to the aer's effects.

37:30.360 --> 37:33.460
Immune to the aer's effects?

37:33.460 --> 37:39.500
Or at least keep it from overloading,
anyway. It won't last long, though.

37:39.500 --> 37:42.440
If you're going to check it out,
you should probably hurry.

37:42.440 --> 37:44.670
If this blastia goes out of control,

37:44.670 --> 37:47.940
it could take out the town,
not just the ruins.

37:48.940 --> 37:51.710
Blastia has the power to protect the city.

37:51.710 --> 37:55.880
So the opposite is just
as possible, don't you think?

37:55.880 --> 37:59.690
I appreciate it. I thank you again.

37:59.690 --> 38:02.380
This is enough thanks for me!

38:08.830 --> 38:12.630
Incidentally, do you live
out here all by yourself?

38:13.500 --> 38:19.110
This is just a lab.
I live somewhere else...

38:19.110 --> 38:21.270
Shut the door, will you?

38:42.460 --> 38:47.270
Your Excellency Commandant Alexei.
The Council has issued a request.

38:47.270 --> 38:51.470
They ask that Lady Estellise be allowed
to attend the upcoming ceremony.

38:51.470 --> 38:52.610
Again?

38:52.610 --> 38:54.710
They claim the celebration
is meaningless without her,

38:54.710 --> 38:57.480
since she may be the successor
to the imperial throne.

38:57.480 --> 38:59.110
Successor?

38:59.110 --> 39:02.670
She is merely the Council's
nominee, nothing more!

39:04.320 --> 39:07.850
Do not allow the Council to
come into contact with Lady Estellise.

39:07.850 --> 39:09.160
Is that clear?

39:09.160 --> 39:11.190
Yes, Sir!

39:11.190 --> 39:15.560
Your Excellency! A messenger
from Ceazontania has arrived.

39:17.160 --> 39:19.360
Ceazontania...

39:21.500 --> 39:24.870
I am Flynn Scifo of
the Ceazontania Brigade.

39:24.870 --> 39:30.810
I've come to attend the ceremony
as Captain Niren Fedrok's proxy.

39:35.350 --> 39:37.940
Why does Fedrok not come himself?

39:39.290 --> 39:43.890
Inside you will find a document
requesting reinforcements.

39:43.890 --> 39:49.300
I ordered all officers ranked captain
or higher to attend this ceremony!

39:49.300 --> 39:52.770
However, Your Excellency,
abnormal aer in a forest near the town

39:52.770 --> 39:57.940
has caused many vicious
monsters to appear!

39:57.940 --> 40:01.140
I humbly beg that you read the request!

40:01.140 --> 40:03.210
When is the ceremony rehearsal?

40:03.210 --> 40:05.700
It will begin shortly.

40:08.680 --> 40:10.840
Your Excellency!

40:12.350 --> 40:15.690
I will dispatch reinforcements
as soon as the ceremony is over.

40:15.690 --> 40:17.990
Your brigade is to hold the fort for now.

40:17.990 --> 40:23.300
The situation is urgent!
The citizens are in danger!

40:23.300 --> 40:24.700
Know your place!

40:24.700 --> 40:29.260
You need only convey my orders to Fedrok!

40:31.000 --> 40:36.270
Return at once. This ceremony is
not for the likes of an amateur Knight.

40:40.510 --> 40:42.780
Flynn Scifo...

40:42.780 --> 40:45.440
The son of Finath Scifo?

40:47.490 --> 40:51.820
I hear you passed the Knights'
recruitment exam with flying colors.

40:51.820 --> 40:56.200
I'm sure your father
would be most delighted.

40:56.200 --> 40:58.200
My father...

40:58.200 --> 41:01.930
Don't go dying a pointless
death, like your father did.

41:01.930 --> 41:05.430
Don't forget that you're
a member of the Knights now.

41:17.850 --> 41:19.370
Flynn...

41:21.620 --> 41:24.120
Lady Estellise...

41:24.120 --> 41:26.460
It's good to see you again.

41:29.360 --> 41:32.870
Thank you for coming
all the way from Ceazontania.

41:32.870 --> 41:36.160
I pray for the citizens' safety.

41:39.870 --> 41:41.360
Thank you, milady.

41:42.340 --> 41:46.180
The imperial capital is maintaining
an uneasy balance right now.

41:46.180 --> 41:51.450
I know it's a lot to ask,
but just hang on a little longer.

41:53.020 --> 41:56.120
I'm glad I was the one sent here.

41:56.120 --> 41:59.830
Yuri would've slugged
His Excellency for sure.

41:59.830 --> 42:01.790
Yuri? Who's that?

42:01.790 --> 42:04.130
Oh, he's just...

42:10.440 --> 42:13.530
Well, then. Please be careful.

42:20.550 --> 42:22.540
He's really botched things.

42:25.320 --> 42:28.880
- Have them taken care of.
- Y-Yes, Sir!

42:51.880 --> 42:54.710
See? I still say taking on
a monster in the forest

42:54.710 --> 42:57.520
would be way better
than this lousy training.

42:57.520 --> 43:01.110
I told you, not until reinforcements
from the capital arrive!

43:28.450 --> 43:30.450
Never seen anything like that before!

43:30.450 --> 43:33.680
The barrier will protect the town! Hurry!

43:40.460 --> 43:42.190
Hurry into town!

43:53.110 --> 43:55.510
Kansuke! Fall back to the town!

44:14.360 --> 44:16.460
Elvin! Fall back!

44:16.460 --> 44:18.500
Yuri! That's enough! Retreat!

44:18.500 --> 44:20.870
My daughter Emma...
She's in the carriage!

44:20.870 --> 44:22.030
Emma...

44:22.030 --> 44:25.300
Emma!

44:51.600 --> 44:53.670
We're going to see your mommy now.

44:53.670 --> 44:55.860
Lambert! Lead the way!

45:13.350 --> 45:16.480
Carry back anyone who's hurt!

45:21.660 --> 45:22.730
Mommy!

45:22.730 --> 45:25.200
Emma... Emma...

45:31.170 --> 45:34.210
Yuri! Retreat back to town!

45:34.210 --> 45:35.470
Yuri!

45:37.540 --> 45:40.610
You sure about this?
There's no money in it for you.

45:40.610 --> 45:43.640
I'll send the bill to your boss.

45:51.660 --> 45:53.350
- Argus!
- John!

45:55.460 --> 45:56.720
Lambert!

46:00.770 --> 46:02.360
Lambert?

46:07.010 --> 46:09.440
Lambert! Wait!

46:09.440 --> 46:11.310
Yuri!

46:11.310 --> 46:12.810
Everyone who can help, come!

46:12.810 --> 46:16.010
Damn! Elvin! Hisca! Let's go!

46:19.550 --> 46:23.320
Damn... Can't make 'em out,
they're all mixed in with the monsters'...

46:24.890 --> 46:27.960
Lambert!

46:27.960 --> 46:31.900
Lambert! Argus!

46:32.800 --> 46:35.530
The aer is even thicker than before.

46:35.530 --> 46:37.640
This is aer?

46:37.640 --> 46:43.710
Normal aer is green, but it apparently
turns red when it's abnormally dense.

46:43.710 --> 46:49.980
Is this aer what's caused the trees
to wither and animals to turn violent?

46:51.720 --> 46:53.550
Hey!

46:53.550 --> 46:55.190
That's our belief.

46:55.190 --> 46:58.550
There's no point in keeping
it under wraps now, jeez!

47:03.930 --> 47:05.660
Boss!

47:09.030 --> 47:11.170
Bastard!

47:11.170 --> 47:12.440
Merzhom!

47:12.440 --> 47:14.770
Stop, Yuri!

47:14.770 --> 47:16.680
Urgh! He never listens!

47:16.680 --> 47:18.440
Be on your guard!

47:30.720 --> 47:32.690
Damn!

47:32.690 --> 47:37.630
Can't believe something this
dangerous appeared so close to town...

47:42.200 --> 47:43.340
Lambert!

47:43.340 --> 47:45.430
Wait, Yuri!

48:26.480 --> 48:28.040
Lambert...

48:40.360 --> 48:43.690
Lambert! Stop, Lambert!

48:50.540 --> 48:52.840
Stop... Lambert...

48:52.840 --> 48:54.330
Lambert...

49:03.450 --> 49:05.820
Lambert!

49:21.670 --> 49:25.100
I'm sorry... Lambert!

49:58.700 --> 50:00.260
Damn it!

50:39.610 --> 50:41.950
I'm sorry, Repede...

50:41.950 --> 50:44.810
Your dad... I had to...

51:15.350 --> 51:17.040
What happened?!

51:17.950 --> 51:20.720
The monsters have made it
all the way to the bridge!

51:20.720 --> 51:22.280
Hisca!

51:26.130 --> 51:29.860
Hisca! Are you all right?! Hisca!

51:29.860 --> 51:34.930
Lambert and the others...
Suddenly they were like monsters...

51:34.930 --> 51:37.000
Then they all...

51:37.000 --> 51:40.170
And then Yuri...

51:43.010 --> 51:44.500
Hisca...

52:04.600 --> 52:06.970
I heard what happened.

52:06.970 --> 52:10.270
Look after Repede.

52:10.270 --> 52:13.530
I bet he's gonna feel
lonely for a good while...

52:15.510 --> 52:17.010
I'm sorry.

52:17.010 --> 52:19.710
Nothin' to apologize about.

52:22.710 --> 52:25.440
Head back to your room now.

52:33.530 --> 52:35.690
Don't catch cold.

52:58.450 --> 53:00.280
W-Wait!

53:32.350 --> 53:36.150
This path sure is rough
on an old guy like me...

53:42.490 --> 53:44.960
What's goin' on this late?

53:55.870 --> 53:57.280
l-It's the truth!

53:57.280 --> 54:01.470
Our blastia suddenly exploded
when we tried to use magic artes!

54:02.310 --> 54:04.810
Explodin' blastia?!

54:06.550 --> 54:08.950
One of Alexei's Royal Guard!

54:09.860 --> 54:12.050
Who's he talkin' to?!

54:13.460 --> 54:14.650
Damn!

54:21.830 --> 54:24.000
What?!

54:24.000 --> 54:27.670
Thank you; I'll take charge of the report.

54:48.790 --> 54:52.530
Looks like things are startin'
ta get a little complicated...

55:37.880 --> 55:40.000
Mister!

55:45.350 --> 55:47.050
You can have this.

55:50.490 --> 55:53.290
Thank you for yesterday.

56:20.220 --> 56:21.620
Flynn...

56:27.960 --> 56:30.860
You sure have it easy,
taking care of some dogs...

56:32.130 --> 56:34.170
What?

56:34.170 --> 56:36.200
I'd say you have it easy.

56:36.200 --> 56:39.200
I hope standing in line at
the ceremony wasn't too tough for you.

56:39.200 --> 56:42.170
Move! I'm busy!

56:43.640 --> 56:47.770
Must be nice getting pampered
just 'cause your dad was a Knight too!

56:55.050 --> 56:59.150
You piece of! I guess that's
the one thing you're good at, huh?!

57:32.460 --> 57:36.560
How many times do we
have to go through this?

57:36.560 --> 57:40.170
Go hit the baths. Then we'll talk!

57:40.170 --> 57:44.840
There's no time to be so laid-back!
We gotta do something!

57:44.840 --> 57:46.630
We can't for now.

57:48.810 --> 57:52.810
He said they can't send reinforcements
until after the ceremony.

57:52.810 --> 57:55.350
His orders are to hold the fort.

57:55.350 --> 57:58.380
I will bring you the documents later.

57:58.380 --> 58:01.190
I see. Thank you.

58:01.190 --> 58:03.860
Did you even explain
the situation to them?!

58:03.860 --> 58:07.830
I did! But this is what
Headquarters decided!

58:07.830 --> 58:11.360
Wait until after the ceremony?
We can't just sit around doing nothing!

58:11.360 --> 58:16.000
I said the same thing!
They just don't see us as a priority!

58:16.000 --> 58:18.470
- There's nothing we can do!
- People have died, you know!

58:18.470 --> 58:20.640
Are you suggesting
I didn't try hard enough?!

58:20.640 --> 58:22.300
That's enough!

58:23.880 --> 58:27.010
Flynn. Sounds like I gave
you an unpleasant task.

58:27.010 --> 58:30.110
That was inconsiderate of me. I apologize.

58:32.350 --> 58:33.520
Captain!

58:33.520 --> 58:35.890
The situation is continuing to worsen.

58:35.890 --> 58:39.950
We won't be able to protect the town
should the monsters attack again!

58:43.030 --> 58:45.860
Tomorrow, we'll investigate the ruins.

58:46.970 --> 58:51.140
You can't be serious! People will
die if we go ahead with this!

58:51.140 --> 58:54.130
We can't disobey an
order from Headquarters!

58:56.810 --> 58:58.970
Thinking of your old man?

59:00.110 --> 59:04.620
My father... he... ignored orders.

59:04.620 --> 59:07.620
Headquarters had
stopped the attack, yet he...

59:07.620 --> 59:10.960
People in the lower quarter were dying.

59:10.960 --> 59:13.360
He did it to protect you and the citizens.

59:13.360 --> 59:16.660
My father died disobeying orders!

59:16.660 --> 59:19.600
There was nothing left of him afterward...

59:19.600 --> 59:23.260
I don't want to make the same
mistake my father did!

59:36.450 --> 59:40.390
Our job is to protect
the people who live here.

59:40.390 --> 59:44.390
That is my duty as a Knight.

59:44.390 --> 59:45.360
Flynn.

59:45.360 --> 59:48.330
Perhaps you should wait until
you've been a Knight for a while

59:48.330 --> 59:53.700
before deciding if your old man's
actions were really a mistake?

59:55.870 --> 01:00:00.270
We leave early tomorrow
morning. Understood?

01:00:00.270 --> 01:00:03.480
Garista. Inform the others.

01:00:03.480 --> 01:00:04.970
Yes, Sir.

01:00:32.440 --> 01:00:37.280
Sorry about earlier.
I didn't know Lambert had died...

01:00:37.280 --> 01:00:38.880
No, I should apologize.

01:00:38.880 --> 01:00:41.810
I was just shocked they refused
to send reinforcements...

01:00:43.210 --> 01:00:47.350
They never brought back my father's body.

01:00:47.350 --> 01:00:49.890
Only a few of his personal effects.

01:00:49.890 --> 01:00:53.830
Once you die, it's all over.
There's nothing left.

01:00:53.830 --> 01:00:57.460
That's why I don't agree
with tomorrow's mission.

01:00:57.460 --> 01:01:00.470
The monsters are
practically on our heels now.

01:01:00.470 --> 01:01:03.030
What happens if they get inside the town?

01:01:03.030 --> 01:01:08.210
The barrier's there.
They can't get inside that easily.

01:01:08.210 --> 01:01:10.610
I'm with the captain on this one.

01:01:10.610 --> 01:01:12.540
We asked for
reinforcements in the first place

01:01:12.540 --> 01:01:15.150
because it's too much
to handle on our own!

01:01:15.150 --> 01:01:17.020
It's our duty to wait!

01:01:17.020 --> 01:01:20.520
More people will get hurt if we do.

01:01:20.520 --> 01:01:23.960
I've had enough of people dying!

01:01:23.960 --> 01:01:26.790
It's all over if we die too!

01:01:41.010 --> 01:01:43.470
I'm going to see Repede.

01:01:51.350 --> 01:01:56.550
Have you reconsidered your decision at all?

01:01:58.220 --> 01:02:03.530
The ceremony will end tomorrow.
Wouldn't it be wiser to wait?

01:02:03.530 --> 01:02:07.300
It'll take 'em days to assemble
a unit and send 'em here.

01:02:07.300 --> 01:02:08.820
Even so...

01:02:09.830 --> 01:02:14.140
Besides, I'd prefer to take care
of this before they arrive.

01:02:14.140 --> 01:02:15.370
Why is that?

01:02:15.370 --> 01:02:19.310
I hear Alexei is really interested in blastia.

01:02:19.310 --> 01:02:22.350
If there is a powerful blastia in the ruins,

01:02:22.350 --> 01:02:25.480
he might order us to bring
it back in working condition.

01:02:25.480 --> 01:02:30.390
It's wreaking havoc with the aer
and turning living creatures violent.

01:02:30.390 --> 01:02:35.460
The citizens, Knights, and livestock
were all harmed while we were away.

01:02:35.460 --> 01:02:39.600
I want to avoid any more casualties.

01:02:39.600 --> 01:02:42.670
I understand.
I'll formulate a route for you.

01:02:42.670 --> 01:02:43.670
Thanks.

01:02:43.670 --> 01:02:48.210
I'm also worried about
taking blastia with us.

01:02:48.210 --> 01:02:52.380
Should the effects of the aer
cause them to go haywire...

01:02:52.380 --> 01:02:57.280
Not having magic artes could
affect the squad's morale, however.

01:02:57.280 --> 01:02:59.350
We still haven't learned to fully control

01:02:59.350 --> 01:03:03.660
the way in which cores
provide blastia with energy.

01:03:03.660 --> 01:03:08.360
I'm sure they activated
a little late last time, that's all.

01:03:08.360 --> 01:03:11.800
All right. We'll take blastia then.

01:03:22.210 --> 01:03:26.680
- It's me, Yuri.
- It's open.

01:03:26.680 --> 01:03:30.280
- What's up?
- Oh, just couldn't sleep...

01:03:30.280 --> 01:03:32.270
That ain't like you.

01:03:37.890 --> 01:03:41.520
- Here. Some juice for you.
- Thanks...

01:03:43.660 --> 01:03:46.430
Your wife and daughter?

01:03:46.430 --> 01:03:49.500
Oh, yeah. They're both dead, though.

01:03:49.500 --> 01:03:54.610
Happened in another incident.
I wasn't able to protect them.

01:03:54.610 --> 01:03:59.610
Back then, I was a firm believer
that the Empire's orders were absolute.

01:03:59.610 --> 01:04:04.950
Even when acting on my own
might've saved their lives...

01:04:04.950 --> 01:04:09.990
Anyway, a lot happened after that,
and I got sent to the middle of nowhere.

01:04:09.990 --> 01:04:14.950
It's actually pretty nice and easy out here,
so far away from the capital...

01:04:16.290 --> 01:04:19.700
It's sure bitin' us in the ass now, though.

01:04:19.700 --> 01:04:25.140
Still, I don't want this
to be a repeat of the past.

01:04:25.140 --> 01:04:27.870
Flynn's old man was really somethin'...

01:04:27.870 --> 01:04:33.650
He was a real negative guy,
but I have a lot of respect for him.

01:04:33.650 --> 01:04:38.610
Guess it boils down to wanting to
personally protect what's dear to you.

01:04:45.190 --> 01:04:47.290
Yes?

01:04:47.290 --> 01:04:50.330
I'm sorry to bother you at this hour...

01:04:50.330 --> 01:04:52.760
What can I do for you, Sir?

01:04:52.760 --> 01:04:54.660
Won't you sit?

01:04:55.700 --> 01:04:59.330
N-No, thank you. We have
an early morning ahead of us...

01:05:00.770 --> 01:05:05.110
You don't seem to agree
with tomorrow's mission.

01:05:05.110 --> 01:05:10.220
I'm a member of the Knights.
My personal feelings are beside the point.

01:05:10.220 --> 01:05:15.520
I, too, am a little troubled
by Captain Fedrok's decision.

01:05:15.520 --> 01:05:19.060
Why does he insist on
placing the brigade in danger?

01:05:19.060 --> 01:05:23.900
I believe we should
obey Headquarters' orders

01:05:23.900 --> 01:05:27.730
and protect the town
until reinforcements arrive.

01:05:29.030 --> 01:05:33.200
It appears you don't take after your father.

01:05:35.110 --> 01:05:39.640
I'd met him once before, you see...

01:05:39.640 --> 01:05:45.670
Captain Fedrok's actions actually
remind me a lot of your father.

01:05:46.680 --> 01:05:50.020
However, His Excellency's
orders are absolute.

01:05:50.020 --> 01:05:54.160
Captain Fedrok should obey orders,
just as your father should have.

01:05:54.160 --> 01:05:55.660
Flynn Scifo.

01:05:55.660 --> 01:05:59.960
Are you still going to go, knowing
you're committing insubordination?

01:05:59.960 --> 01:06:04.200
As a Knight, I will obey
the person in charge of this town.

01:06:04.200 --> 01:06:07.210
I don't fully agree with him,

01:06:07.210 --> 01:06:11.010
but I also wish to learn the meaning
behind the captain's words.

01:06:11.010 --> 01:06:12.770
Good night.

01:06:15.980 --> 01:06:21.820
A shame. He might have made
a fine servant for His Excellency...

01:06:31.500 --> 01:06:33.330
Are you all right?

01:06:33.330 --> 01:06:37.130
I hafta drink for my dead pal too!

01:06:40.310 --> 01:06:43.970
- Okay! Time to drink more!
- You need to go home.

01:06:48.280 --> 01:06:49.940
Let's go back.

01:07:20.280 --> 01:07:22.850
Our brigade will now follow the river

01:07:22.850 --> 01:07:25.550
and enter the ruins on the lake.

01:07:25.550 --> 01:07:27.820
Our objective is to investigate the ruins

01:07:27.820 --> 01:07:31.160
and identify and resolve
the cause of the aer disturbance.

01:07:31.160 --> 01:07:33.660
I'd prefer to wait for reinforcements
from the imperial capital,

01:07:33.660 --> 01:07:35.830
but this is a matter of emergency.

01:07:35.830 --> 01:07:41.830
The city will be in grave danger
if we don't stop the aer now.

01:07:41.830 --> 01:07:44.770
We must protect the people!

01:07:46.670 --> 01:07:50.630
So, umm... Shall we go?

01:08:03.390 --> 01:08:04.790
Yuri.

01:08:13.660 --> 01:08:17.800
What's the matter?
Why are you up so early?

01:08:17.800 --> 01:08:21.310
Are you guys going somewhere dangerous?

01:08:21.310 --> 01:08:23.310
Sheesh, where'd you hear that?

01:08:23.310 --> 01:08:26.800
Don't worry. You know how tough I am.

01:08:31.450 --> 01:08:33.210
Captain...

01:08:39.520 --> 01:08:43.460
C'mon. Don't look like a bunch of grumps.

01:08:47.100 --> 01:08:52.100
We'll be gone for a bit. Wait for us,
and don't leave the barrier, okay?

01:08:52.100 --> 01:08:56.810
Life will be back to normal soon.
Just hang on a little longer.

01:08:56.810 --> 01:08:58.300
Let's go.

01:09:26.040 --> 01:09:30.130
Talk about reckless. They have
no idea what they're up against...

01:09:31.810 --> 01:09:34.880
After we went and warned 'em, too...

01:09:34.880 --> 01:09:37.320
That's Niren for ya...

01:09:37.320 --> 01:09:42.220
But, y'know, havin' them owe
us one doesn't sound half-bad...

01:09:42.220 --> 01:09:44.660
You serious?

01:09:44.660 --> 01:09:48.460
You need to report to the Don! Scram!

01:09:48.460 --> 01:09:49.990
Yeah, yeah!

01:09:49.990 --> 01:09:52.360
Well, take care.

01:10:20.220 --> 01:10:21.790
Captain?

01:10:21.790 --> 01:10:26.260
Yurgis. Give your blastia a try.

01:10:26.260 --> 01:10:29.130
Huh? Yes, Sir...

01:10:41.010 --> 01:10:43.210
What the?!

01:10:57.160 --> 01:10:59.660
It's the aer here.

01:10:59.660 --> 01:11:01.830
We can't use our blastia?!

01:11:01.830 --> 01:11:04.300
That's where these come in.

01:11:04.300 --> 01:11:07.640
These formulas will keep
them from overloading.

01:11:07.640 --> 01:11:10.110
I made enough copies for everyone.

01:11:10.110 --> 01:11:14.480
They don't last long, though.
Use 'em as a last resort.

01:11:14.480 --> 01:11:17.950
You knew our blastia would
go out of control, Sir?!

01:11:17.950 --> 01:11:21.150
Yeah. That's why I said
this is an emergency.

01:11:21.150 --> 01:11:25.190
We can't let the town's
Barrier Blastia go haywire.

01:11:25.190 --> 01:11:27.180
Let's move.

01:11:28.190 --> 01:11:33.190
- You're only telling us now?!
- Could've prepared us before we left!

01:11:35.500 --> 01:11:38.330
My bad. I forgot.

01:11:40.200 --> 01:11:42.270
Huh?!

01:11:42.270 --> 01:11:45.040
- You're unbelievable!
- You gotta be kidding me!

01:11:45.040 --> 01:11:49.640
Is it really okay to leave
this old guy in charge?

01:11:52.980 --> 01:11:55.320
Shut up! Let's go! Come on!

01:11:58.690 --> 01:12:02.830
I guess this explains why
we haven't run into any monsters...

01:12:02.830 --> 01:12:05.300
Hey, I dunno about this...

01:12:05.300 --> 01:12:08.370
Are we gonna end up like that too?

01:12:08.370 --> 01:12:11.770
Stay alert! There's no
telling what might happen!

01:12:36.360 --> 01:12:38.560
Frozen Arrows, ready!

01:12:38.560 --> 01:12:41.030
Don't hit David now! Fire!

01:12:47.140 --> 01:12:48.700
Pull him out!

01:13:08.490 --> 01:13:11.120
Away from the swamp! Hurry!

01:13:26.380 --> 01:13:31.950
That swamp monster seemed
to react to sound and movement.

01:13:31.950 --> 01:13:34.650
We'll split into two teams now.

01:13:34.650 --> 01:13:38.360
One will cross the bridge and enter
the ruins; the other will give support.

01:13:38.360 --> 01:13:41.330
The support team will provide
cover all the way to the entrance,

01:13:41.330 --> 01:13:46.520
secure a return route, and then wait
for the infiltration team to return.

01:13:47.360 --> 01:13:48.630
Captain!

01:13:51.670 --> 01:13:54.700
Let me avenge Lambert.

01:13:55.770 --> 01:13:57.940
I'm counting on it.

01:13:57.940 --> 01:14:00.810
- Yurgis! Assign the teams!
- Yes, Sir!

01:14:00.810 --> 01:14:03.050
Those with crossbows, you're on support.

01:14:03.050 --> 01:14:06.680
Those with swords, axes, or
defensive artes, you're on infiltration.

01:14:06.680 --> 01:14:10.280
Support team!
Use the formulas the captain gave you!

01:14:13.560 --> 01:14:14.960
Flynn!

01:14:18.300 --> 01:14:19.660
Get over here!

01:14:22.330 --> 01:14:23.870
- Yurgis!
- Sir!

01:14:23.870 --> 01:14:25.500
Over here, Flynn.

01:14:30.310 --> 01:14:33.680
Thought you didn't agree with this?

01:14:33.680 --> 01:14:35.540
It's still my duty.

01:14:57.130 --> 01:14:59.000
Everyone ready?

01:15:23.360 --> 01:15:25.160
There it is! Hurry!

01:15:27.700 --> 01:15:29.860
You're dealing with us!

01:15:39.210 --> 01:15:40.440
Let's go!

01:16:07.140 --> 01:16:10.600
Now comes the real challenge. Stay sharp!

01:16:29.030 --> 01:16:30.320
Captain!

01:16:36.770 --> 01:16:38.370
It's flowing from there...

01:16:38.370 --> 01:16:40.340
Let's follow it to the source!

01:17:06.630 --> 01:17:08.150
What is it?

01:18:42.460 --> 01:18:45.390
- Careful, Flynn.
- Yes, Sir.

01:18:49.130 --> 01:18:51.970
Even further down, huh...

01:18:51.970 --> 01:18:54.030
There's the entrance.

01:19:13.890 --> 01:19:16.330
Oww...

01:19:16.330 --> 01:19:18.360
Yo.

01:19:18.360 --> 01:19:20.330
Merzhom!

01:19:24.640 --> 01:19:27.500
You're gettin' old, Niren...

01:19:30.170 --> 01:19:32.700
Right back at ya.

01:19:34.480 --> 01:19:40.520
Hey, Yuri. You look like
your back's against the wall.

01:19:40.520 --> 01:19:42.710
You sure like to butt in, huh?

01:19:44.520 --> 01:19:46.390
You have no charm at all!

01:19:46.390 --> 01:19:51.660
If the town bites the dust,
we're outta work too!

01:19:51.660 --> 01:19:54.700
Plus some of my men need avengin'.

01:19:54.700 --> 01:19:56.630
Let's finish this once and for all.

01:19:56.630 --> 01:19:58.470
Captain!

01:19:58.470 --> 01:20:01.700
The pain's gone now. I'll be fine.

01:20:06.710 --> 01:20:10.880
- Take off your blastia.
- Huh? But...

01:20:10.880 --> 01:20:14.150
If it goes off, it'll take us all out!

01:20:14.150 --> 01:20:15.710
Y-Yes, Sir!

01:20:38.640 --> 01:20:43.810
- This is it, all right.
- I'm countin' on you two!

01:20:58.800 --> 01:21:00.460
Niren!

01:21:33.730 --> 01:21:35.530
Swords don't work!

01:21:48.610 --> 01:21:49.870
Flynn!

01:22:10.600 --> 01:22:13.300
Yuri! Cut the red cords!

01:22:31.150 --> 01:22:33.650
- Yuri!
- Right!

01:22:46.770 --> 01:22:47.930
Let's go!

01:22:50.640 --> 01:22:53.880
There's no end to 'em! Go on ahead!

01:22:53.880 --> 01:22:55.710
I appreciate it!

01:23:18.540 --> 01:23:20.800
Now that's big...

01:23:56.110 --> 01:23:57.840
Oww...

01:24:00.040 --> 01:24:01.850
Oh, no!

01:24:01.850 --> 01:24:04.310
No! Help!

01:24:17.530 --> 01:24:20.390
Yuri! I'll toss you up there!

01:24:23.670 --> 01:24:25.130
Come on!

01:24:55.100 --> 01:24:58.030
Yuri!

01:25:24.360 --> 01:25:27.160
I take it you're all right?

01:25:27.160 --> 01:25:28.500
Yeah...

01:25:58.730 --> 01:26:02.890
So this thing's sucking up
aer to act in place of a core?

01:26:07.640 --> 01:26:11.940
That's a pretty big gizmo.

01:26:11.940 --> 01:26:15.350
- You okay?
- Lost one of my men.

01:26:15.350 --> 01:26:17.550
I'm sorry to hear it.

01:26:17.550 --> 01:26:19.620
Who built this?

01:26:19.620 --> 01:26:21.780
We can look into it later.

01:26:23.150 --> 01:26:25.950
This ought to stop the flow of aer.

01:26:32.000 --> 01:26:36.360
What is it?

01:27:03.360 --> 01:27:04.880
It stopped!

01:27:17.270 --> 01:27:18.430
Chastel!

01:27:39.000 --> 01:27:41.500
- This is not good!
- Yuri!

01:27:41.500 --> 01:27:42.830
Let's get outta here!

01:27:45.640 --> 01:27:47.190
Hold this!

01:28:01.380 --> 01:28:04.020
- What are you doing?!
- Captain! Look!

01:28:04.020 --> 01:28:05.610
This core...

01:28:07.020 --> 01:28:08.150
Later!

01:28:38.320 --> 01:28:42.310
Yuri!

01:28:50.330 --> 01:28:52.200
Chastel! Chastel!

01:28:52.200 --> 01:28:54.860
She's okay! She's breathing!

01:28:56.340 --> 01:28:57.810
Captain!

01:29:07.280 --> 01:29:08.880
Give me your hand!

01:29:14.660 --> 01:29:16.520
We'll hold you!

01:29:21.060 --> 01:29:23.700
I'll help you! Just hold on!

01:29:23.700 --> 01:29:24.800
Damn it!

01:29:24.800 --> 01:29:26.840
It's no use. Go.

01:29:26.840 --> 01:29:28.440
Shut up!

01:29:28.440 --> 01:29:31.780
Give me your hand, dammit!

01:29:31.780 --> 01:29:34.840
Can't do much of anything now...

01:29:36.110 --> 01:29:38.680
That can be fixed! Give me your hand!

01:29:38.680 --> 01:29:39.620
Yuri...

01:29:39.620 --> 01:29:42.390
I can't reach him at all!
Can't we use anything else?!

01:29:42.390 --> 01:29:44.320
Yuri!

01:29:50.230 --> 01:29:54.990
You know it's too late for me.
Go save everyone who can be saved.

01:30:07.480 --> 01:30:09.000
Take this.

01:30:17.020 --> 01:30:20.150
Flynn. Look after everyone.

01:30:25.160 --> 01:30:29.500
Become a great Knight.
Surpass your old man.

01:30:34.370 --> 01:30:38.500
No! Captain! Captain!

01:30:42.510 --> 01:30:44.100
Go...

01:30:47.020 --> 01:30:48.610
Farewell.

01:32:35.860 --> 01:32:38.850
Chastel... Thank goodness...

01:32:41.560 --> 01:32:43.120
Oww...

01:32:47.200 --> 01:32:48.710
We're alive...

01:32:48.710 --> 01:32:50.870
Yeah... It's over.

01:32:50.870 --> 01:32:54.180
Oh, you're awake.

01:32:54.180 --> 01:32:56.980
Huh? Where's the captain?

01:33:02.020 --> 01:33:04.710
Flynn! Where's the captain?!

01:33:13.830 --> 01:33:15.350
Yuri...

01:33:16.470 --> 01:33:19.460
He went out in style.

01:34:24.870 --> 01:34:30.670
I know it's a formality, but it seems
silly when there's nothing inside...

01:34:30.670 --> 01:34:33.610
The captain said making
his mission his priority

01:34:33.610 --> 01:34:36.050
was what kept him
from protecting his family.

01:34:36.050 --> 01:34:40.180
He said he respected your dad.

01:34:53.660 --> 01:34:57.270
What, you're still not done yet?

01:34:57.270 --> 01:35:01.540
You were ordered to
hold the fort, you know!

01:35:01.540 --> 01:35:05.880
How dare he harm the brigade
His Excellency gave him...

01:35:05.880 --> 01:35:10.780
Incompetent fool. Did he think he was
a hero of the people or something?

01:35:10.780 --> 01:35:14.820
How could you work for a lousy captain...

01:35:14.820 --> 01:35:15.950
Yuri!

01:35:15.950 --> 01:35:17.320
Stop, Yuri!

01:35:17.320 --> 01:35:20.520
How dare you waltz in here
now and trash talk him!

01:35:20.520 --> 01:35:22.990
You little!

01:35:38.040 --> 01:35:41.670
It's time to carry the casket out.
Lend a hand, you two.

01:36:12.280 --> 01:36:14.800
What kind of brigade is this?!

01:37:05.190 --> 01:37:06.860
Captain...

01:37:06.860 --> 01:37:11.630
When the captain died,
I think he did leave something behind.

01:37:11.630 --> 01:37:16.370
He's the reason everyone
is still alive. Right?

01:37:16.370 --> 01:37:22.970
So I'm absolutely sure your dad
left something behind when he died too!

01:37:25.150 --> 01:37:29.450
Salute Captain Niren Fedrok
of the Imperial Knights!

01:38:21.700 --> 01:38:23.260
Yuri...

01:38:24.540 --> 01:38:26.870
It isn't over yet.

01:38:59.310 --> 01:39:01.940
We found it planted inside the ruins.

01:39:04.810 --> 01:39:07.840
Only you use that type of core.

01:39:12.050 --> 01:39:16.560
Why did you do it?! Were you
trying to destroy the town?!

01:39:16.560 --> 01:39:18.190
Don't be silly.

01:39:18.190 --> 01:39:23.670
Those ruins were simply a test
bed for a new type of blastia.

01:39:23.670 --> 01:39:25.370
A new type of blastia?

01:39:25.370 --> 01:39:26.800
That's right.

01:39:26.800 --> 01:39:30.610
Our way of life demands that
we control aer and blastia,

01:39:30.610 --> 01:39:35.610
yet excavation is our only method
for obtaining crystallized aer cores.

01:39:35.610 --> 01:39:38.710
But if we could create an
artificial replacement for cores,

01:39:38.710 --> 01:39:43.720
it'd free us from the fear of monsters
and usher in even greater prosperity.

01:39:43.720 --> 01:39:45.890
But then your blastia went out of control,

01:39:45.890 --> 01:39:49.860
so you tried to destroy it all
and take the brigade out with it!

01:39:49.860 --> 01:39:55.670
At present, we don't even have
full control over normal blastia.

01:39:55.670 --> 01:40:00.330
Luckily for us, that's how we were
able to bring back that core as proof.

01:40:03.040 --> 01:40:07.180
Actually, there were other experiments
with some measure of success.

01:40:07.180 --> 01:40:11.040
There were casualties then too, of course...

01:40:15.150 --> 01:40:17.450
You don't mean!

01:40:17.450 --> 01:40:19.890
You have my sympathies.

01:40:32.500 --> 01:40:37.100
It appears a blastia explosion
is in order here, too.

01:41:02.230 --> 01:41:04.030
That hurts...

01:41:30.190 --> 01:41:32.460
You're really starting to annoy me...

01:41:48.880 --> 01:41:50.870
Damn it...

01:41:55.680 --> 01:42:00.060
Flynn! It's sink or swim!
Create an opening!

01:42:00.060 --> 01:42:01.280
Got it!

01:42:09.670 --> 01:42:11.720
Such nonsense!

01:42:15.370 --> 01:42:17.170
Take this!

01:42:31.050 --> 01:42:33.040
That's...

01:42:35.120 --> 01:42:37.680
The captain's blastia.

01:42:50.170 --> 01:42:53.540
Captain... It's over.

01:43:23.640 --> 01:43:24.870
Hisca...

01:44:00.180 --> 01:44:02.850
Seeing me off?

01:44:02.850 --> 01:44:06.140
Yeah. It's not like me at all.

01:44:07.480 --> 01:44:10.020
Looks like everyone else is leaving too.

01:44:10.020 --> 01:44:14.360
It's only natural, with
the Empire abandoning this place.

01:44:14.360 --> 01:44:19.030
Plus all the guild guys are long gone.

01:44:19.030 --> 01:44:23.330
Having the captain around must've
been why Merzhom liked it here too.

01:44:23.330 --> 01:44:28.200
Yeah, with the captain gone,
I don't think I'm cut out for the Knights.

01:44:30.610 --> 01:44:33.480
Sorry. I leave the clean-up work to you.

01:44:33.480 --> 01:44:37.150
Vice Captain Yurgis
quietly accepted our report

01:44:37.150 --> 01:44:41.380
that said Garista Luodor died
in a blastia explosion accident.

01:44:41.380 --> 01:44:46.160
It seems he was suspicious of Garista too,
after the captain filled him in.

01:44:46.160 --> 01:44:49.850
That's why he's given his silent approval.

01:44:52.960 --> 01:44:57.830
You're tough, Flynn.
I can never hope to be like you.

01:44:57.830 --> 01:45:00.440
Likewise, Yuri.

01:45:00.440 --> 01:45:04.640
Choosing to make it in the world
all alone... That's you, all right.

01:45:04.640 --> 01:45:10.210
I'll try to find what the captain
sought by staying with the Knights.

01:45:10.210 --> 01:45:12.480
That's what he asked me to do, too.

01:45:15.320 --> 01:45:18.880
Sorry. I shouldn't have
said "alone", Repede.

01:45:23.830 --> 01:45:26.400
Take good care of it.

01:45:26.400 --> 01:45:27.990
See ya.

01:45:29.570 --> 01:45:31.000
Yeah.

01:45:40.440 --> 01:45:42.270
See you later.

01:45:52.960 --> 01:45:58.030
Separated from you
and searching for myself

01:45:58.030 --> 01:46:03.200
I walked thousands of nights

01:46:03.200 --> 01:46:08.140
What to aim for, who to trust

01:46:08.140 --> 01:46:12.810
Each time I made a vow, I wavered again

01:46:12.810 --> 01:46:22.950
The bell echoing in the morning
haze isn't far, not far at all

01:46:22.950 --> 01:46:33.200
Sometimes being yourself
also means being alone

01:46:33.200 --> 01:46:38.330
Does light follow to the ends of shadow

01:46:38.330 --> 01:46:43.370
and does shadow follow
to the ends of light?

01:46:43.370 --> 01:46:48.510
If the clouds grow
dark and the sky begins to cry

01:46:48.510 --> 01:46:53.520
I will ring a bell and look for you

01:46:53.520 --> 01:46:59.320
The world is black or white, peace or war

01:46:59.320 --> 01:47:04.390
heads or tails, you and I,
light and dark, ups and downs

01:47:04.390 --> 01:47:14.140
Amid it all, will we someday meet
and hold each other's hand?

01:47:14.140 --> 01:47:19.110
Does light follow to the ends of shadow

01:47:19.110 --> 01:47:24.210
and does shadow follow
to the ends of light?

01:47:24.210 --> 01:47:29.280
If I can live life with a smile

01:47:29.280 --> 01:47:36.380
then I will ring a bell to let you know
